  end note

  note top of Q_S04_BUSINESS_GROUP_2
    This is computed field as 
    we did it for Q-S04 in ECB
  end note

  note top of Q_S04_BORROWER
    This is computed field as 
    we did it for Q-S04 in ECB
  end note

  note right of Q_S05
    This is the same derived question COUNTERPARTY_CHARACTERISTICS/PARENT
  end note

  note right of Q_S06
    This is the same lookup question LOOKUP as Q-S06 of the ECB form and 
    below are the same behavior of errors we added in 
    * If the legal entity name does not belong to a Business Group and error message will be show
        "Please select a company belonging to the same Business Group of the subsidiary or contact RMPM team to add this counterparty to the Business Group"
    * If the legal entity (LOOKUP field) remains empty, an error message will be shown
        "Please choose a reference entity"
    * If the legal entity name is different from the parent company name saved in RMPM but it still belongs to the same business group an information message will occur:
        "Information: changing the parent company's name must be exceptional and related to specific cases. If the parent company in RMPM is not accurate, please proceed to the modifications required in RMPM"
    * When correctly completed, then
    ** FED form is finished
    ** Flag "Leveraged Flag" = "Calculation at BG or another LE Level" (flags: fedLeveragedFlag = CALCULATION_AT_BG_OR_OTHER_LE)

  end note

  note left of GENERAL_OBLIGOR_AND_UTILITIES_PATH_QUESTION_1
  **Setting of fedLeveragedFlag**
  {{
    skinparam backgroundColor transparent
    skinparam shadowing false
    start
    if (Is Highly Secured Debt 100% of\nBorrower/Business Group Total Debt?) then (yes)
      :fedLeveragedFlag =\nFED not Leveraged;
    else (no)
      if (Q01 == Yes\nOR ceFedLeverageRatio >= ceThresholdPerPolicyBasedOnSector\nOR ceFedLeverageRatio < 0) then (yes)
        if (Q01 == Yes\nOR PATH_QUESTION_5 == Yes) then (yes)
          :fedLeveragedFlag =\nFED Leveraged High Risk;
        else (no)
          if (PATH_QUESTION_3 == Yes\nOR PATH_QUESTION_4 == Yes\nOR PATH_QUESTION_2 == Yes) then (yes)
            :fedLeveragedFlag =\nFED Leveraged Low Risk;
          else (no)
            if (raAdjustedEbitda < 0\nAND adjustedFundedTotalDebt < 0) then (yes)
              :fedLeveragedFlag =\nFED Leveraged Low Risk;
            else (no)
              if (raAdjustedEbitda < 0) then (yes)
                :fedLeveragedFlag =\nFED Leveraged High Risk;
              else (no)
                if (raFedLeverageRatio >= raThresholdPerPolicyBasedOnSector) then (yes)
                  :fedLeveragedFlag =\nFED Leveraged High Risk;
                else (no)
                  :fedLeveragedFlag =\nFED Leveraged Low Risk;
                endif
              endif
            endif
          endif
        endif
      else (no)
        :fedLeveragedFlag =\nFED not Leveraged;
      endif
    endif
    stop
  }}
end note

  note right of Q_E01
    **Q0 "Threshold for Escalation" is not a question.**
    It is the escalationThreshold field displayed on
    FINANCIAL_TABLE_1 (x6, x7 for Utilities).

    Q_E01 is Yes/No, mandatory, filled by the analyst.
    It is only reached when the escalation tests apply;
    "hidden" in the BR == never reached in the walk.
  end note

  note right of Q_E02
    Reached only from Q_E01 = Yes.
    The BR "field hidden if Q1 is set at No" is expressed
    as routing, not as a visibility rule - an unreached
    question is blank, which is the same outcome.
  end note

  note right of Q_E03
    **Computed. Value rules, first match wins:**

    field ceFedLeverageRatio range [>0 .. <escalationThreshold]  -> NO
    Q_E01 is NO   -> YES
    Q_E02 is YES  -> YES
    Q_E01 is YES  -> NO

    **There is deliberately no "*" catch-all.**
    An NA (undefined) ratio matches no rule and the question
    keeps no value - this is the "= empty" outcome.
    The last line is the BR's "Else No": it is reachable only
    when Q_E01 was actually asked, which means the ratio was defined.

    **OPEN - Clara:** the written cascade in Section 1.1 falls through
    to "Else No" for an NA ratio; the flowchart says "empty".
    Empty means the test did not apply, No means it applied and passed.
    Authored here per the flowchart.

    **OPEN - Clara:** in the flowchart the True/False labels on the
    "Threshold for Escalation < 0" diamond are transposed - as drawn,
    both branches of the ">= 6x" diamond reach the same box.
    Authored here per the Section 1.1 text (<6x and >0 -> No).
  end note
@enduml